[gd_scene format=3]

; The Underice, under the Mere (map offset (270.5, -121)): a drowned cave between the lake bed and the bedrock, roofed
; with old ice. Everything here is under water: the pilgrim comes down the shaft from the lake bed sunk (Ballast), and
; moves only by sinking and rising. Curtains of ice hang from the roof nearly to the floor; ridges of rock rise nearly to
; the roof; the way west goes under one and over the next, past the hulk of a machine that drowned here, to a low door
; in the west wall: the Vault's pool, from beneath. Back up the shaft to the Mere by rising.

